  "findings": [
    "Original capability RED0/1 rejects propagate=true before provider/compiler work; only the first TS case was reached. It is not a compiler-result failure.",
    "Initial R2 compile failed E0505 because a tree cursor still borrowed the returned tree; R3 drops that cursor, and both actual TS/JS propagation fixtures pass. Raw source/output and unchanged inputs are preserved.",
    "Initial R4 qualification passed576/0/7 plus all actual gates and Clippy, but the additional source-role RED0/1 proved a provider comment-token claim could wrongly seed an unrelated previously-unused declaration. Only the first comment variant was reached in RED. R6 repeated577/0/7 and all actual/Clippy gates on the deny-list predicate. Additional R7 binding RED0/1 passed the first three variants but admitted an arrow parameter and again pruned the unrelated function. Final R8 uses positive expression-role admission/default refusal for unknown roles and repeats all20contracts with four role variants plus the entire selected regression/actual scope.",
    "Finite explicit function propagation uses exact AST/entity and self-bound provider definitions/references. It removes only owned standalone call statements and private dependency candidates newly unused after those source regions disappear. Private cycles can prune together; surviving reported/possible consumers and exported dependencies remain protected. Unrelated already-unused functions are not swept.",
    "Reported references, captured graph evidence and lexical/literal candidates retain their distinct roles and original observations; identical physical removals are emitted once. Missing/empty/omitted/truncated/foreign/unbound proofs refuse, rather than returning empty complete coverage.",
    "All 20 new default contract cases pass: both epochs/force, cycles/live/export, argument dependencies, duplicate/nested calls, BOM/UTF16, authority/paths/protocol shapes/stale/deadline, exact declaration/statement/module/file/physical-byte boundaries and real owned byte-verification/approval/apply/recovery. Quota probes at 2000 files and16MB reach an intentionally unavailable definition; they do not claim a complete maximum-size provider workflow.",
    "One actual propagation Rust test covers two owned TS/JS compiler/provider/apply/recovery fixtures. Legacy actual declaration/file-usage gates add four Rust tests/eight owned fixtures. Counts across attempts/gates are nonadditive.",
    "All captured physical files are checked at preparation before/after provider work. This does not lease future consumers or repeat semantic queries at apply; ordinary guarded plan preconditions remain. completefalse, exhaustiveCompilerProoffalse and remainingUsagesMayBreaktrue retain unknown dynamic/external/omitted/differently-configured consumers.",
    "General propagation outside this finite TS/JS function-module policy, other declaration/language/file cases, full R1-R9/IDE/hosted/platform acceptance, main merge and release remain open. Earlier whole-native Windows failures are preserved, not replaced by this selected run."
  ],
